--
N5008 [temp.param]/4, [temp.arg.nontype]/1-2: a non-type template parameter may
have reference type, its argument designating a static-storage object (an
address constant).  CBMC drops the declarator's `&` (treating `const T &empty`
as a value parameter), valuifies the reference argument, and fails to
instantiate util/reference_counting.h's
`template <typename T, const T &empty = T::blank>` -- the root of the
ref_expr_set.cpp / rename_symbol.cpp / replace_symbol.cpp goto-cc cascade.  The
to_constant_expr abort in the instance-name builder is fixed (template_suffix no
longer forces a scalar-constant conversion on a non-scalar argument); full
reference-NTTP support remains.  Flip to CORE once supported.
